# Elegy Acolyte's Void: Black Lotus is a nonland permanent, and sacrificing it for mana (to pay for the Acolyte itself)
# makes it leave the battlefield this turn, so at the beginning of Bot1's end step the "if" holds and a 2/2 colorless
# Robot artifact creature token is created (compare the first Elegy Acolyte scenario, where nothing left and no Robot
# came). The Mox Jet stays, the Lotus is in the graveyard.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Black Lotus
Elegy Acolyte
Island x4
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Hand.Elegy Acolyte.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Jet; Elegy Acolyte; Robot Token
Bot1.Battlefield.Robot Token.Token = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Robot Token.Types = Artifact; Creature
Bot1.Battlefield.Robot Token.Power = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Robot Token.Toughness = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Robot Token.Colors = (absent)
Bot1.Graveyard = Black Lotus
